          "definition": "<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt17\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/political\" title=\"political\">political</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/philosophy\" title=\"philosophy\">philosophy</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/opposed\" title=\"opposed\">opposed</a> to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/separation\" title=\"separation\">separation</a> of a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/religious\" title=\"religious\">religious</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/group\" title=\"group\">group</a> (church) and a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/government\" title=\"government\">government</a> (state), especially the belief held by those in 19th-century <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/England\" title=\"England\">England</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/opposed\" title=\"opposed\">opposed</a> to separating the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Anglican\" title=\"Anglican\">Anglican</a> church from the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/civil\" title=\"civil\">civil</a> government, or the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/separation%20of%20church%20and%20state\" title=\"w:separation of church and state\" class=\"extiw\">separation of church and state</a>. <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r90144991\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt18\">.mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}</style>"
